      "body": "EVIDENCE. The cancellation flow requires consumers to answer a survey question and select additional choices before they can continue toward cancellation.\nLEGAL REASONING. The complaint alleges the \"Cancel plan\" action does not cancel anything and instead starts a multi-step process with unnecessary friction before recurring charges can be stopped.\nSTATED LAW. FTC Act Section 5(a), 15 U.S.C. 45(a); ROSCA Section 4(3), 15 U.S.C. 8403(3).",
