    {
      "body": "EVIDENCE. The final checkout page collects card information and uses bright checkout buttons while cancellation-fee and auto-renewal disclosures appear only in smaller text below the payment path.\nLEGAL REASONING. The complaint alleges Shutterstock obtained billing information before clearly and conspicuously disclosing material negative-option terms, defeating express informed consent.\nSTATED LAW. FTC Act Section 5(a), 15 U.S.C. 45(a); ROSCA Section 4(1)-(2), 15 U.S.C. 8403(1)-(2).",
